# =====================================================================
# OPTIONAL: split-ECS blueprint (ships DISABLED — do not just include)
# =====================================================================
# Project default (Saman's core-model decision): ECS is OFF. Upstreams
# geolocate by the NODE's IP, which is exactly the foreign-node model:
# game/CDN edges are picked for the node's location, where the tunnel
# actually exits.
#
# The split-ECS idea from the 2026 research is narrower: for pure
# matchmaking/CDN domains it can help to show the upstream the
# PLAYER's /24 instead, while sanction-bypass domains keep resolving
# by the node's location. Expected gain is small and title-dependent;
# that is why this is a blueprint, not a default.
#
# To experiment (on a real node, never blind):
#   1. Create a second upstream group whose servers carry your
#      SmartDNS build's client-subnet option, e.g.:
#        server-tls 1.1.1.1 -group edge -exclude-default-group -subnet 203.0.113.0/24 -subnet-all-query-types
#        server-https https://cloudflare-dns.com/dns-query -group edge -exclude-default-group -subnet 203.0.113.0/24 -subnet-all-query-types
#        server-quic 1.1.1.1 -group edge -exclude-default-group -subnet 203.0.113.0/24 -subnet-all-query-types
#        server-h3 h3://1.1.1.1/dns-query -group edge -exclude-default-group -subnet 203.0.113.0/24 -subnet-all-query-types
#      and enable ECS forwarding per your build's documentation
#      (`smartdns -h` / the release notes of YOUR version — the exact
#      flag differs between releases; verify before deploying).
#      (This exact form — DoT+QUIC+H3 edge group with the player's /24 —
#      is what the reference nodes run in production since v1.15.)
#   2. Route ONLY matchmaking/CDN domain-sets to it:
#        nameserver /domain-set:cod/edge
#        domain-set -name psn -file /etc/ofogheamn-dns/lists/psn.domains
#        nameserver /domain-set:psn/edge
#        domain-rules /domain-set:psn/ -speed-check-mode ping,tcp:443 -response-mode fastest-ip
#      and REMOVE those domains from any other set that also routes
#      them (a domain in two routed sets follows the first set that
#      claims it — the PlayStation domains ship in lists/psn.domains
#      for exactly this reason; do not duplicate them into
#      gaming.domains).
#      (keep the gaming set and everything else on the default
#      node-located path).
#   3. Measure with `ofogheamn-dns region` + in-game ping before and
#      after. If the median does not improve for YOUR ISP/title,
#      revert — ECS also leaks the player's subnet to upstreams.
# =====================================================================
